1495:    * out of Babylon's frustum culling (their vertex shader moves them to the
1496:    * ground, away from their own bounds), so without this every loaded
1497:    * object's shadow is submitted every frame - most of them behind the
1498:    * camera. `OutOfView` is measured against a frustum widened past the
1499:    * projection's reach (RenderSystem), so a caster just off screen still
1500:    * draws the shadow that pokes into view.
1501:    */
